  <h2>Study routes</h2>
  <p><a href="https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/electronic-structure/excitation-spectra-and-optical-properties/E708B2F729C1961D9A9D598FCDBAF656">Martin, <cite>Electronic Structure</cite>, Chapter 21</a> connects TDDFT, dielectric response, time propagation, molecular and crystal optics, and limitations of the adiabatic approximation. Publisher access may be required.</p>
  <p><a href="https://archive.nptel.ac.in/courses/115/101/115101009/">IIT Bombay / NPTEL, <cite>Ideas and Methods in Condensed Matter Theory</cite></a> provides a compact conceptual route before implementation-specific response methods. Its opening module derives the retarded response kernel, explains analyticity and dispersion relations, and connects the imaginary response to equilibrium fluctuations through the fluctuation–dissipation theorem before moving to interacting condensed-matter examples. The course assumes undergraduate quantum and statistical physics; it does not teach DFPT or TDDFT code details, and its response conventions must be matched to the notation used here.</p>
  <p><a href="https://octopus-code.org/main/tutorials/2-optical-response/">Octopus Optical Response tutorials</a>, maintained by the Theory Department of the Max Planck Institute for the Structure and Dynamics of Matter, make the distinct time-propagation, Casida, and Sternheimer routes concrete and include triplet and symmetry cases. They suit readers already able to run an Octopus ground-state calculation; their molecular examples, grids, and code inputs are not universal parameter prescriptions or a proof that an excitation spectrum is converged.</p>

  <h2>Boundary of this page</h2>
  <p>This page does not merge DFPT, TDDFT, GW, and BSE into one method. It does not identify a Kohn–Sham gap with an optical or quasiparticle gap, or one broadened spectrum with a fully converged excitation calculation.</p>

  <aside class="review-note">
    <p><strong>Review note.</strong> Scope follows the Theory systematic-review report and Martin second edition. The IIT Bombay/NPTEL response module and official Cambridge and Octopus destinations were rechecked through 4 August 2026. Course completion does not validate a response observable or a numerical spectrum.</p>
  </aside>
</BaseLayout>
